//? Title: RetinaNet sigmoid focal loss and shared dense heads
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Verify tensor focal values and gradients, ignored-anchor matching and full RetinaNet graph structure, then fit and evaluate the complete compact source detector with a visible Adam loop and paired BN-state checkpoints.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/retinanet.cpp`.

> The method

RetinaNet combines feature pyramids with shared class/box towers and focal modulation of dense foreground/background imbalance. Every class is an independent sigmoid channel, and moving backbone normalization state is part of the selected fitted model.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/retinanet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/retinanet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/retinanet_concept.tikz > build/retinanet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/retinanet_concept.svg build/retinanet_concept.dvi > build/retinanet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
