> Nine anchors per cell and ignored matches

Each P3–P7 cell has three scales (1, cube-root 2, cube-root 4) and three
height/width ratios (.5, 1, 2), ordered level, row, column, scale, ratio.
Pixel strides are 8/16/32/64/128 and base sides double by level. Tensor powers
can differ by one Float32 rounding unit from the source host cube root; the
Float64 independent coordinate oracle checks every coordinate within 1e-12.
Anchors are unclipped until decoding. Distinct forced matching gives every
truth a different anchor even at low IoU, then adds IoU >=.5 matches. Unmatched
anchors with IoU >=.4 are ignored; remaining anchors are background. Positive
box coding uses unit variances. The loss is masked focal plus positive
Smooth-L1 with beta 1/9, divided by batch positives floored at one. An empty
positive set still trains background focal loss, unlike SSD hard-negative mining.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/retinanet_anchors.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  m::TensorDetectionScenes data;
  data.images = n::zeros({1, 64, 64, 1});
  data.boxes = {n::tensor({0., 0., 10., 10.}, {1, 4})};
  data.labels = {n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{1})};
  const auto a = n::tensor({0., 0., 10., 10., 0., 0., 10., 22., 30., 30., 40., 40.}, {3, 4});
  const auto t = m::MakeRetinaTargets(a, data, {0}, 2);
  if (t.positive.to_vector<int>() != std::vector<int>{1, 0, 0} ||
      t.weights.to_vector<int>() != std::vector<int>{1, 0, 1})
    return 1;
  const auto anchors = m::RetinaAnchors({8, 4, 2, 1, 1}, 8., n::DType::Float64);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  for (int i = 0; i < 9; ++i) {
    const double y1 = anchors.at({i, 0}), x1 = anchors.at({i, 1}), y2 = anchors.at({i, 2}),
                 x2 = anchors.at({i, 3});
    const std::array<dm::graphics::RGB, 3> colors = {
        {{37, 99, 235}, {22, 163, 74}, {220, 38, 38}}};
    plot.lines({x1, x2, x2, x1, x1}, {y1, y1, y2, y2, y1},
               i % 3 == 0 ? "scale " + std::to_string(i / 3 + 1) : "", colors[i / 3]);
  }
  plot.title("Nine first-cell RetinaNet anchors")
      .x_label("pixel x")
      .y_label("pixel y")
      .x_limits(-8, 16)
      .y_limits(-8, 16)
      .size(900, 900)
      .margins(90, 30, 60, 60);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  plot.save_svg("build/retinanet_anchors.svg");
  std::print(
      "Compact64: {} anchors. Fixture IoUs1,10/22,0 give positive, ignored and background "
      "masks[1,0,0]/[1,0,1]. Equal x/y pixel scaling preserves anchor shapes.\n",
      anchors.shape()[0]);
}
```
