> Full-weight architecture and compact fitting

The full model uses feature-only ResNet50, a linear 256-channel FPN and shared
four-layer classification/regression towers. P6 comes from original C5;
P7 comes from ReLU(P6). Predictor/tower kernels use normal standard deviation
.01 and classifier bias logit(.01). Full counts are 37,968,692 learned scalars
and 53,120 BN-state scalars, with 76,725 anchors at 640 pixels. The source's
128-pixel full-weight backward check below computes all 195 learned tensor
derivatives. It is an initialized graph check, without pretraining or fitting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
  n::models::RetinaNetConfig cfg;
  cfg.image_size = 128;
  cfg.update_stats = false;
  const auto net = n::models::RetinaNet(
      p, state, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 128 * 128 * 3)).reshape({1, 128, 128, 3}), cfg,
      true);
  if (p.count() != 37968692 || state.count() != 53120 || net.anchors != 3069)
    return 1;
  const auto g =
      n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.logits)) + n::mean(n::square(net.deltas)), p.parameters());
  if (g.size() != 195)
    return 1;
  for (const auto &v : g)
    if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v)).item()))
      return 1;
  std::print("Full-weight128-pixel graph: {} learned scalars, {} state scalars, {} anchors "
             "and {} defined finite learned tensor derivatives. At640 pixels, tensor anchors "
             "number{}. No fitted benchmark is claimed.\n",
             p.count(), state.count(), net.anchors, g.size(),
             n::models::RetinaAnchors({80, 40, 20, 10, 5}).shape()[0]);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full-weight128-pixel graph: 37968692 learned scalars, 53120 state scalars, 3069 anchors and 195 defined finite learned tensor derivatives. At640 pixels, tensor anchors number76725. No fitted benchmark is claimed.
// result_end

The bounded fit uses 64 fit/16 validation scenes made from the first 2048
MNIST training digits, seed 11; eight test scenes use the first 512 official
test digits, seed 22. The compact source network has ResNet18 with widths
divided by eight, a 32-channel FPN and shared towers: 346,246 learned scalars
plus 1,200 backbone BN-state scalars. This report uses 64-pixel scenes and base
anchor side eight (the source's larger scene run uses 128 pixels/base16).
It fits the entire network with explicit Adam(.001), batch four, 32 epochs,
512 updates and `.00005*sum(kernel²)`. All leaves are warmed before constructing
Adam. Biases/normalization affines are optimized but excluded from kernel L2.
Validation AP50 selects paired learned-parameter and moving-state files.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/retinanet_scenes.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  std::vector<n::Tensor> boxes(scenes.boxes.begin(), scenes.boxes.begin() + 8);
  const auto preview = n::models::DrawDetectionBoxes(n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 8),
                                                     boxes, {.1, 1., .2});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(preview, "build/retinanet_scenes.png", 4, 0., 1., 4, 1., 2);
  std::int64_t objects = 0;
  for (const auto &b : scenes.boxes)
    objects += b.shape()[0];
  std::print("80 generated training/validation scenes; {} accepted digits. Preview: first "
             "eight training scenes with tight green boxes.\n",
             objects);
}
