\image(figures/retinanet_detections.png)
\caption(Actual held-out compact RetinaNet detections in red, with green target outlines. Extra boxes and localization mistakes remain visible; colour does not certify correct classification.)
\alttext(Eight held-out MNIST-derived scenes with green truth and red decoded RetinaNet boxes.)


> Conclusion

The compact run selects epoch18 at validation AP50 .114848. Test AP50 is .021629, AP75 is zero and AP50:95 is .003207, with the 100/image cap reached in every scene. This schedule has poor held-out detection quality; the dense false positives in the gallery show the gap between decreasing training loss and generalization.

The independent focal oracle, ignored-band fixture and full-weight backward check precede a bounded whole-network fit. Actual training scenes and restored held-out detections are saved locally. This is an instructional compact digit detector, not pretrained COCO accuracy.

> References

- [Lin et al. (2017), Focal Loss for Dense Object Detection](https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.02002).
- [Lin et al. (2017), Feature Pyramid Networks for Object Detection](https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.03144).
